        {
          "mdr_text_key": "16129784789",
          "text_type_code": "Description of Event or Problem",
          "patient_sequence_number": "0",
          "text": "It was reported that the Extravascular (EV) lead exhibited noise which was detected as Non-Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia. Reprogramming was done and the EV lead remains in use. The patient is a participant in a clinical study. No patient complications have been reported as a result of this event. It was further reported that the noise on the lead that was detected as Non-Sustained Ventricular Tachycardia was probably due to Electromagnetic Interference (EMI) on the Extravascular Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillator (EV-ICD). During a device check, respiration and arm movement did not provoke the noise. The device was reprogrammed to avoid the oversensing. The device remains in use."
        },
